plan Pending
title   Pending Plan amendments, merged once proven
status  proposed
goal
    Plan changes found while building wait here, unmerged, until building proves them right. Each
    decision names the Plan record it changes, the change, why, and the evidence that would prove
    it. One is merged into its Plan only once that evidence holds and the user says yes, then
    removed from here with the merge commit noted on the Epic.
decisions
    D1  @plan.Operations.O3: a cancel during a send leaves the call Held
        Change O3's phrase that says a cancel settles a call on the wire, to match @spec.WriteLanes.R14
        as revised: the call follows its own ending and stays Held. **Why:** the phrase came from the
        old design's `HeldThisTurn`, which is about the `cancel` concurrency policy (the R4 entry in
        code:workflow/specs/spec-log.md). **Proven by:** P4's production lane passing the suite's
        cancel-on-wire cases (PAY-12, PAY-15, LANE-04). Found in @task.V3.T7.
    D2  @plan.Machines.O3: a denied or unhandled ending's lane-only change is published
        Change O3's "Unhandled or denied events publish nothing" to "publish nothing of their own; an
        ending admitted in that turn publishes its lane-only change", as @spec.Turn.R19 and the same
        outcome's step-one rule already say. **Why:** otherwise rows stay stale after a denied ending
        (the Invariant audit's G7, code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/invariant-audit-2026-11-11.md).
        **Proven by:** P3's Turn cases for @spec.Turn.I15 showing the row change. Found in @task.V3.T42.
    D3  @plan.Runtime.O6: disposal invokes nothing
        Drop "and invokes what the lane table promotes" from O6's disposal paragraph, which the same
        outcome contradicts ("from its start nothing is invoked"); @spec.Actors.R22 and
        @spec.Actors.I30 follow the second reading. **Why:** the audit's G17. **Proven by:** P3's
        disposal cases (`o6.*` wrong runtimes) staying green on round 14. Found in @task.V3.T42.
    D4  @plan.Operations.O3: a refused ending is redelivered once only for a mapper throw
        Narrow O3's "a pre-commit defect is not retried for that input" to match @spec.WriteLanes.R10:
        a refused ending is redelivered once when its mapper threw, and never otherwise. Round-14
        redelivers any refused ending once, a prototype deviation. **Proven by:** P4's production
        turn passing TURN-01 with the issue count asserted. Found in @task.V3.T8.
